From 426be42c4b9c7a4d757c8204b3560725d6eb852c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rustcc-build <rustcc@localhost>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 02:10:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.x (1.13.6): transparent base-member access via auto-Deref
 + RTTI/layout fixes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Transparent base-member access for `class D : B { ... }`:
`self.member` now reaches B's fields and methods directly (no
`self.__base.` prefix), and `&D` upcasts to `&B`. The parser
synthesizes two ordinary trait impls per derived class —

    impl Deref    for D { type Target = B; fn deref(&self)     -> &B     { &self.__base } }
    impl DerefMut for D {                  fn deref_mut(&mut self) -> &mut B { &mut self.__base } }

— stored in `ast::Class::deref_impls` as complete AST items. They flow
through the normal def-collection / resolve / lowering paths (no custom
HIR synthesis): expansion fills their `DUMMY_NODE_ID`s, def_collector
visits them, `index_crate` registers them as owners via the Class walk,
`lower_item_ref` emits their `ItemId`s, and `resolve_item` resolves
them as module-scope siblings. Field/method access and upcasting then
fall out of Rust's existing autoderef — emitted code is just a field
projection at offset 0.

Plumbing: `ast::Class` gains `deref_impls`; the AST visitor, parser
(`build_cxx_class_deref_impls`), def_collector, ast_lowering
(`lower_item_ref` + the two struct/pretty destructures), and resolve
are updated. New `sym::DerefMut`.

RTTI + layout fixes (a class deriving from a NON-polymorphic base used
to fail to link / miscompute its vptr):
- `is_polymorphic_cpp_class` (itanium + the cxx_bridge mirror) now
  recurses the base chain: a `#[rustc_cxx_base]` to a non-polymorphic
  base does NOT make the derived class polymorphic. Fixes a dangling
  `_ZTI` reference ("undefined symbol: typeinfo for Base") when neither
  class has virtuals.
- `has_polymorphic_base` (layout) now requires the base to be
  polymorphic, so a class that introduces the *first* virtual on a
  plain base correctly adds its own vptr instead of assuming the base
  provides one (was: garbage field offsets at runtime).
- `emit_typeinfo` emits a non-polymorphic base's `_ZTS`/`_ZTI` on
  demand (idempotently, recursing the chain) so a polymorphic derived
  class's `__si_class_type_info` resolves.

Validated: transparent field read/write + method calls + upcast;
multi-level inheritance; generic bases; field shadowing (derived wins);
non-poly-base + first-virtual-in-derived links and computes correct
offsets. Probe matrix 11/11.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
